{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstruction"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.exists_nonzero_equivariant_into_trivial_of_trivial_source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.exists_nonzero_equivariant_into_trivial_of_trivial_source","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L263-L272","doc":"**The theorem is about the SIGN source, not about the target being small.** With\nthe *trivial* representation as source, nonzero equivariant linear maps into the\ntrivial representation obviously exist — the identity is one.  Without this a reader\ncould suspect the conclusion came from the target rather than from Schur. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.sq_functional_is_equivariant_and_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.sq_functional_is_equivariant_and_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L248-L261","doc":"**The linearity hypothesis is load-bearing.** The QUADRATIC functional `x ↦ x²` is\nS₃-equivariant into the trivial representation — `(signR g * x)² = x²` — and is not\nidentically zero.  So the theorem above genuinely needs linearity, and the surviving\ncoupling is through `μ̄²` (equivalently `|μ̄|`), matching\n`MilnorSignRepObstruction.muBarFamily_sq_invariant`.\n\nStated over `ℤ` so that \"not identically zero\" is a concrete, checkable claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.muBar_cannot_carry_nucleon_triple_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.muBar_cannot_carry_nucleon_triple_channel","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L228-L244","doc":"**A nucleon triple's channel cannot be linear in `μ̄` — the escape closed.**\n\nGiven any species assignment (only `p`/`n` exist), `exists_identical_pair` supplies a pair\nof identical components; `hflip` is the invariance under swapping them; and the channel is\nthen forced to zero, contradicting a nonzero measured value.\n\nThe corpus's measured cumulants require `tripleMutual = −(b₃ + 3b₂) = −8.09991876` MeV `≠ 0`\n(probe `b3_brunnian_count_channel_probe.py`), so `hne` is discharged by data.  Note the\nspecies assignment is *arbitrary* — this is not a statement about ³H or ³He in particular. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.linear_in_muBar_vanishes_of_identical_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.linear_in_muBar_vanishes_of_identical_pair","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L210-L226","doc":"**The obstruction needs only ONE transposition — the minimal form.**\n\nIf a channel is a linear functional `T` of the antisymmetric invariant, and there is a\nsingle component swap under which `μ̄` flips sign while the channel does not, then the\nchannel vanishes.  No group action, no S₃, no representation theory: linearity gives\n`T(−μ̄) = −T(μ̄)`, the invariance gives `T(−μ̄) = T(μ̄)`, and the two force `T(μ̄) + T(μ̄) = 0`.\n\n`hflip` is the physical content: *swapping two identical nucleons flips `μ̄` (it is totally\nantisymmetric) and leaves the mutual energy of the triple unchanged (they are identical\nparticles, so the state is the same).* ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.exists_identical_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.exists_identical_pair","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L203-L208","doc":"**Only two species, so any three nucleons include two of the same kind.**  Pigeonhole\non `Fin 3 → Fin 2`, decided exhaustively (8 species assignments). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.muBar_cannot_carry_symmetric_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.muBar_cannot_carry_symmetric_channel","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L155-L170","doc":"**A nonzero symmetric three-body channel cannot be linear in `μ̄`.**\n\nIf `T` is an S₃-equivariant linear functional of the antisymmetric invariant whose\nvalue on `μ̄` is the required channel, and that channel is **nonzero**, contradiction.\n\nThe corpus's measured cumulants require `tripleMutual = -(b₃ + 3b₂) = -8.09991876`\nMeV `≠ 0` (probe `b3_brunnian_count_channel_probe.py`), so the hypothesis `hne` is\ndischarged by data and the conclusion bites. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.equivariant_linearMap_to_trivial_eq_zero_of_neZero_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.equivariant_linearMap_to_trivial_eq_zero_of_neZero_two","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L139-L151","doc":"Convenience version, 2-torsion-freeness discharged from `[NoZeroDivisors R]` +\n`[NeZero (2 : R)]` (e.g. `ℤ`, `ℚ`, or any integral domain of characteristic `≠ 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.equivariant_linearMap_to_trivial_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.equivariant_linearMap_to_trivial_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L115-L137","doc":"**The triple-channel D2 obstruction.** Any S₃-equivariant `R`-linear map from the\nsign representation (the line spanned by `μ̄(123)`) into the **trivial** representation\nis ZERO.\n\nThis is the companion of `equivariant_linearMap_eq_zero` with the target changed from\nthe pair-channel module `Fin 3 → R` to a scalar carrying the trivial action — the\ntarget a *symmetric* three-body channel actually lives in. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.sign_equivariant_scalar_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.sign_equivariant_scalar_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorSignRepObstructionTripleChannel.lean#L102-L113","doc":"**Core computation.** A ring element `c` that transforms in the SIGN representation\nwhile its target carries the **trivial** action — `signR g * c = c` for every `g` —\nvanishes, provided `R` has no 2-torsion.\n\nProof: a transposition has `signR = -1`, so `-c = c`, hence `c + c = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}